From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 22:54:05 +0530
Subject: drm/buddy: fall through to kernel drm_buddy.h on pre-gpu_buddy kernels

The upstream split of the buddy allocator moved the core allocator
(struct gpu_buddy and the gpu_buddy_* API) into <linux/gpu_buddy.h> and
left <drm/drm_buddy.h> as a thin, print-only overlay.

On kernels that predate this split the full allocator (struct drm_buddy
and friends) still lives in the kernel's own <drm/drm_buddy.h>, and
backport-include/linux/gpu_buddy.h remaps the gpu_buddy_* API onto the
kernel's drm_buddy_* symbols.

The problem is that the copied print-only overlay shares the include
guard __DRM_BUDDY_H__ with the kernel's full header.  Because the
backport include path is searched before the kernel headers, an
guard and shadows the kernel header.  struct drm_buddy is therefore
never defined, leaving struct gpu_buddy incomplete:

error: field 'mm' has incomplete type

Guard the print-only overlay behind BPM_GPU_BUDDY_H_AVAILABLE.  When the
kernel does not natively provide gpu_buddy, fall through via
drm_buddy (and the drm_buddy_* helpers) become available.

Signed-off-by: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
---
 include/drm/drm_buddy.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/drm/drm_buddy.h b/include/drm/drm_buddy.h
--- a/include/drm/drm_buddy.h
+++ b/include/drm/drm_buddy.h
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
  */
 
 #ifndef __DRM_BUDDY_H__
+
+#if defined(BPM_GPU_BUDDY_H_AVAILABLE) || defined(CPTCFG_BUILD_XE_DRM_BUDDY)
 #define __DRM_BUDDY_H__
 
 #include <linux/gpu_buddy.h>
@@ -15,4 +17,8 @@
 void drm_buddy_block_print(struct gpu_buddy *mm,
 			   struct gpu_buddy_block *block,
 			   struct drm_printer *p);
+#else
+#include_next <drm/drm_buddy.h>
+#endif /* BPM_GPU_BUDDY_H_AVAILABLE || CPTCFG_BUILD_XE_DRM_BUDDY */
+
 #endif
